---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ModelInfo from '../../../components/ModelInfo.astro';
import ToolMeta from '../../../components/ToolMeta.astro';
import ParamsDrawer from '../../../components/ParamsDrawer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Heterostructures | Lab" description="Interactive stacking solver for the electromagnetic modes of layered heterostructures: surface plasmons at planar Drude interfaces, with normalized Economou axes and physical unit controls.">
  <section class="widget-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/lab/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Lab</a>
      <h1>Hetero<span class="gradient-text">structures</span></h1>
      <p class="widget-hero__subtitle">
        An interactive stacking solver for the electromagnetic modes of layered
        heterostructures. Pick a module below, build your stack, and explore its
        response with normalized Economou axes and physical unit controls.
      </p>
      <ToolMeta slug="heterostructures" name="Heterostructures" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <ModelInfo status="Beta">
    <dl>
      <dt>Model</dt>
      <dd>Two modules over planar stratified media. <strong>Surface plasmons</strong> solves the TM dispersion relation of single boundaries and thin films from matched Drude dielectric layers. <strong>Layered structure</strong> uses the transfer-matrix method (TMM) for reflection/transmission spectra and field profiles of arbitrary multilayer stacks.</dd>
      <dt>Assumptions</dt>
      <dd>Infinite, flat, parallel interfaces; isotropic and local dielectric functions; TM polarization for the plasmon branch; metals described by a Drude model &epsilon;(E) = &epsilon;<sub>&infin;</sub> &minus; (&omega;<sub>p</sub>/E)<sup>2</sup>.</dd>
      <dt>Validity</dt>
      <dd>Exact within the transfer-matrix formalism for any stack of isotropic homogeneous layers. The plasmon dispersion uses the lossless Drude branch.</dd>
      <dt>Limitations</dt>
      <dd>No in-plane structure or roughness, no spatial dispersion (nonlocality), no absorption in the dispersion-pole branch. The PyRAMIDS module assumes the emitting layer is transparent (LDOS is undefined inside an absorbing source layer).</dd>
      <dt>References</dt>
      <dd>E. N. Economou, Phys. Rev. <strong>182</strong>, 539 (1969); P. Yeh, <em>Optical Waves in Layered Media</em> (Wiley, 1988).</dd>
    </dl>
  </ModelInfo>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="module-bar card" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Heterostructure module">
        <span class="module-bar__label">Module</span>
        <div class="module-bar__grid">
          <button type="button" class="module-card active" id="module-surface-plasmons" role="radio" aria-checked="true">
            <span class="module-card__name">Surface plasmons</span>
            <span class="module-card__desc">Planar Drude interfaces &amp; thin films</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="module-card" id="module-layered-structure" role="radio" aria-checked="false">
            <span class="module-card__name">Layered structure</span>
            <span class="module-card__desc">Transfer-matrix R/T spectra &amp; field profiles</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="module-card" id="module-pyramids" role="radio" aria-checked="false">
            <span class="module-card__name">PyRAMIDS</span>
            <span class="module-card__desc">Dipole emission &amp; LDOS in stratified media</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Fixed excitation slot: reserves the same row for every module so the
           parameter/result boxes never shift when switching. Only PyRAMIDS
           shows it (visibility toggled by the module switcher). -->
      <div class="excitation-bar excitation-bar--hidden" id="pr-excitation">
        <div class="param excitation-param excitation-above">
          <div class="param-header"><label>Excitation</label></div>
          <div class="plot-tabs" id="pr-exc-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Excitation">
            <button class="plot-tab" type="button" data-prexc="pw" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Plane wave</button>
            <button class="plot-tab active" type="button" data-prexc="dip" role="radio" aria-checked="true">Dipole</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="widget-layout" id="module-panel-surface-plasmons">
        <ParamsDrawer>
        <aside class="controls card">
          <div class="panel-title-row">
            <h3>Parameters</h3>
            <div class="preset-actions" aria-label="Quick layer presets">
              <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-dmd" title="Dielectric-metal-dielectric">DMD</button>
              <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-mdm" title="Metal-dielectric-metal">MDM</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param">
            <div class="param-header">
              <label>Layers</label>
              <span class="param-readout" id="layer-count">2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stepper-row">
              <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="remove-layer" title="Remove layer" aria-label="Remove layer">
                <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>
              </button>
              <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="add-layer" title="Add layer" aria-label="Add layer">
                <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14"/><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="stack-preview" id="stack-preview" aria-label="Layer stack preview"></div>

          <div class="layer-editor" id="layer-editor"></div>

          <h3>Plot range</h3>
          <div class="param">
            <span class="axis-section-label">Vertical axis</span>
            <div class="axis-control-row axis-control-row--vertical">
              <div class="segmented segmented--compact axis-kind-tabs" id="y-axis-kind-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Vertical axis quantity">
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-y-kind="energy" role="radio" aria-checked="true" aria-label="Photon energy" title="Photon energy">Energy</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-y-kind="frequency" role="radio" aria-checked="false" aria-label="Frequency" title="Frequency">Freq.</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-y-kind="wavelength" role="radio" aria-checked="false" aria-label="Photon wavelength" title="Photon wavelength">&lambda;</button>
              </div>
              <div class="segmented segmented--compact unit-tabs" id="y-unit-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Vertical axis unit">
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-y-kind="energy" data-y-unit="ev" role="radio" aria-checked="true">eV</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-y-kind="energy" data-y-unit="wp" role="radio" aria-checked="false">&omega;/&omega;<sub>p</sub></button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-y-kind="frequency" data-y-unit="hz" role="radio" aria-checked="false" hidden>Hz</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-y-kind="wavelength" data-y-unit="lambda-nm" role="radio" aria-checked="false" hidden>nm</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-y-kind="wavelength" data-y-unit="lambda-um" role="radio" aria-checked="false" hidden>&mu;m</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-y-kind="wavelength" data-y-unit="lambda-lp" role="radio" aria-checked="false" hidden>&lambda;/&lambda;<sub>p</sub></button>
              </div>
              <select class="wp-reference-select" id="wp-reference-select" aria-label="Plasma frequency reference" hidden></select>
            </div>
            <div class="range-grid range-grid--compact">
              <label>
                <span id="y-min-label">Photon energy min</span>
                <input type="number" class="param-number" id="y-min" step="0.01">
              </label>
              <label>
                <span id="y-max-label">Photon energy max</span>
                <input type="number" class="param-number" id="y-max" step="0.01">
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param">
            <span class="axis-section-label">Horizontal axis</span>
            <div class="axis-control-row">
              <span>Parallel momentum</span>
              <div class="segmented segmented--compact unit-tabs" id="x-unit-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Horizontal axis unit">
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-x-unit="nm" role="radio" aria-checked="true">nm<sup>-1</sup></button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-x-unit="cm" role="radio" aria-checked="false">cm<sup>-1</sup></button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-x-unit="kp" role="radio" aria-checked="false">k/k<sub>p</sub></button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="range-grid">
              <label>
                <span id="x-min-label">Parallel momentum min</span>
                <input type="number" class="param-number" id="x-min" step="0.001">
              </label>
              <label>
                <span id="x-max-label">Parallel momentum max</span>
                <input type="number" class="param-number" id="x-max" step="0.001">
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="theory-note">
            Single-boundary TM pole:
            k = (&omega;/c) [ &epsilon;<sub>1</sub>&epsilon;<sub>2</sub> /
            (&epsilon;<sub>1</sub> + &epsilon;<sub>2</sub>) ]<sup>1/2</sup>.
            Drude layers use &epsilon;(E) = &epsilon;<sub>&infin;</sub> -
            (&omega;<sub>p</sub>/E)<sup>2</sup> for the lossless dispersion branch.
          </p>

          <button type="button" class="reset-btn" id="reset-parameters">Reset</button>
        </aside>
        </ParamsDrawer>

        <main class="lab-main">
          <section class="chart-panel card">
            <div class="chart-header">
              <div>
                <span class="chart-title" id="chart-title">Surface plasmons dispersion relation</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-options" aria-label="Reference lines">
              <label class="check-row check-row--compact">
                <input type="checkbox" id="show-light" checked>
                <span>Light line</span>
              </label>
            <label class="slope-control">
              <input type="checkbox" id="show-tailored" checked>
              <span>Slope / c</span>
              <input type="range" class="slope-slider" id="tailored-slope-slider" aria-label="Line slope (fraction of c)" value="0.35" step="0.01" min="0" max="2">
              <input type="number" class="param-number param-number--sm" id="tailored-slope" value="0.35" step="0.01" min="0">
            </label>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-wrap" id="chart-wrap">
              <canvas id="dispersion-chart" aria-label="Surface plasmon dispersion chart"></canvas>
              <div class="chart-tooltip" id="chart-tooltip" hidden></div>
          </div>
          <div class="chart-interface-control">
            <span>Layers</span>
            <div class="interface-tabs" id="interface-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Displayed layers"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="chart-legend" id="chart-legend"></div>
            <div class="download-bar">
              <span class="download-label">Export</span>
              <button id="dl-png" class="dl-btn" title="Download plot as PNG">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/><path d="m21 15-5-5L5 21"/></svg>
                PNG
              </button>
              <button id="dl-csv" class="dl-btn" title="Download all plotted branches as CSV">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                CSV
              </button>
              <button id="dl-share" class="dl-btn" title="Copy shareable link to clipboard">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg>
                Share
              </button>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="model-note card">
            <div class="model-note__header">
              <span>Notes</span>
              <span id="model-summary">single interface</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            <strong>Selected layer branch:</strong> TM surface-plasmon pole.
            The plotted branch is the real, lossless single-interface mode for
            the currently selected adjacent layers.
          </p>
          <p>
            Symmetric DMD and MDM presets use the coupled thin-film branches
            when the whole film layer is displayed. DMD means
            Dielectric-Metal-Dielectric; MDM means Metal-Dielectric-Metal.
          </p>
          </section>

          <section class="references-card card">
            <div class="references-card__header">
              <h3>References</h3>
              <div class="figure-preset-actions" aria-label="Economou figure presets">
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig1" title="Economou Fig. 1 single interface">Fig. 1</button>
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig2" title="Economou Fig. 2 retardation guide">Fig. 2</button>
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig3" title="Economou Fig. 3 insulating film between metals">Fig. 3</button>
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig4" title="Economou Fig. 4 metal film in vacuum">Fig. 4</button>
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig5" title="Economou Fig. 5 Swihart geometry">Fig. 5</button>
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig6" title="Economou Fig. 6 two metal films">Fig. 6</button>
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig7" title="Economou Fig. 7 two dielectric films">Fig. 7</button>
                <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="preset-fig8" title="Economou Fig. 8 three metal films">Fig. 8</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p>
              E. N. Economou, <em>Surface Plasmons in Thin Films</em>,
              Phys. Rev. 182, 539, published 10 June 1969.
              DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.182.539" target="_blank" rel="noopener">10.1103/PhysRev.182.539</a>.
            </p>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== Layered structure (Transfer Matrix Method) module ===== -->
      <div class="widget-layout" id="module-panel-layered-structure" hidden>
        <ParamsDrawer>
        <aside class="controls card">
          <div class="panel-title-row">
            <h3>Stack</h3>
            <div class="preset-actions" aria-label="Quick stack presets">
              <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="tmm-preset-bragg" title="Quarter-wave Bragg mirror">Bragg</button>
              <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="tmm-preset-fp" title="Fabry-Perot cavity (half-wave defect)">Fabry&ndash;P&eacute;rot</button>
              <button type="button" class="preset-chip" id="tmm-preset-ar" title="Single quarter-wave antireflection film">AR film</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="tmm-ends">
            <label class="layer-field">
              <span>Substrate n<sub>s</sub> (inc)</span>
              <input type="number" class="param-number" id="tmm-n-sub" step="0.01" min="0.05" value="1">
            </label>
            <label class="layer-field">
              <span>Cladding n<sub>c</sub> (out)</span>
              <input type="number" class="param-number" id="tmm-n-clad" step="0.01" min="0.05" value="1.5">
            </label>
          </div>

          <div class="param">
            <div class="param-header">
              <label>Layers</label>
              <span class="param-readout" id="tmm-layer-count">2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stepper-row">
              <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="tmm-remove-layer" title="Remove layer" aria-label="Remove layer">
                <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>
              </button>
              <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="tmm-add-layer" title="Add layer" aria-label="Add layer">
                <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14"/><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="tmm-stack" id="tmm-stack-preview" aria-label="Layer stack preview"></div>
          <div class="layer-editor" id="tmm-layer-editor"></div>

          <h3>Illumination</h3>
          <div class="param">
            <div class="axis-control-row">
              <span>Polarization</span>
              <div class="segmented segmented--compact" id="tmm-pol-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Polarization">
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-pol="TE" role="radio" aria-checked="true">TE (s)</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-pol="TM" role="radio" aria-checked="false">TM (p)</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="param" id="tmm-angle-control">
              <span class="axis-section-label" id="tmm-angle-label">Angle of incidence (&deg;)</span>
              <div class="tmm-slider-row">
                <input type="range" class="slope-slider" id="tmm-angle-slider" aria-labelledby="tmm-angle-label" min="0" max="90" step="0.5" value="0">
                <input type="number" class="param-number param-number--sm" id="tmm-angle" step="1" min="0" max="90" value="0">
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="tmm-spectrum-controls">
            <span class="axis-section-label">Horizontal axis</span>
            <div class="segmented segmented--compact" id="tmm-xunit-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Horizontal axis quantity">
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-xunit="nm" role="radio" aria-checked="true">Wavelength</button>
              <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-xunit="ev" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Photon energy</button>
            </div>
            <span class="axis-section-label" id="tmm-range-label">Wavelength (nm)</span>
            <div class="range-grid range-grid--compact">
              <label><span>Min</span><input type="number" class="param-number" id="tmm-lam-min" step="10" min="10" value="400"></label>
              <label><span>Max</span><input type="number" class="param-number" id="tmm-lam-max" step="10" min="10" value="800"></label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="tmm-wavelength-control" hidden>
            <span class="axis-section-label">Wavelength (nm)</span>
            <div class="tmm-slider-row">
              <input type="range" class="slope-slider" id="tmm-lam-slider" aria-label="Wavelength (nm)" min="200" max="1200" step="1" value="600">
              <input type="number" class="param-number param-number--sm" id="tmm-field-lam" step="5" min="10" value="600">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="param" id="tmm-field-margins" hidden>
            <span class="axis-section-label">Sampling margin (nm)</span>
            <div class="range-grid range-grid--compact">
              <label><span>Substrate</span><input type="number" class="param-number" id="tmm-margin-sub" step="50" min="0" value="300"></label>
              <label><span>Cladding</span><input type="number" class="param-number" id="tmm-margin-clad" step="50" min="0" value="300"></label>
            </div>
          </div>

          <button type="button" class="reset-btn" id="tmm-reset">Reset</button>
        </aside>
        </ParamsDrawer>

        <main class="lab-main">
          <section class="chart-panel card">
            <div class="chart-header">
              <div class="segmented segmented--compact tmm-mode-tabs" id="tmm-mode-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Chart mode">
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-mode="spectrum" role="radio" aria-checked="true">Spectrum</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-mode="angles" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Angles</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-mode="fields" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Fields</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-mode="structure" role="radio" aria-checked="false">Structure</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-options" id="tmm-spectrum-options">
              <label class="check-row check-row--compact"><input type="checkbox" id="tmm-show-r" checked><span>Reflectance &rho;</span></label>
              <label class="check-row check-row--compact"><input type="checkbox" id="tmm-show-t" checked><span>Transmittance &tau;</span></label>
              <label class="check-row check-row--compact"><input type="checkbox" id="tmm-log"><span>Log scale</span></label>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-options" id="tmm-field-options" hidden>
              <label class="check-row check-row--compact"><input type="checkbox" id="tmm-show-abs" checked><span>|F(z)|</span></label>
              <label class="check-row check-row--compact"><input type="checkbox" id="tmm-show-re"><span>Re[F(z)]</span></label>
              <label class="check-row check-row--compact"><input type="checkbox" id="tmm-show-index" checked><span>Index profile</span></label>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-options" id="tmm-structure-options" hidden>
              <span class="axis-section-label">Quantity</span>
              <div class="segmented segmented--compact" id="tmm-quantity-tabs" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Profile quantity">
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn active" data-quantity="nk" role="radio" aria-checked="true">n, &kappa;</button>
                <button type="button" class="seg-btn" data-quantity="eps" role="radio" aria-checked="false">&epsilon;</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-wrap" id="tmm-chart-wrap">
              <canvas id="tmm-chart" aria-label="Transfer-matrix chart"></canvas>
              <div class="chart-tooltip" id="tmm-chart-tooltip" hidden></div>
            </div>
            <div class="chart-legend" id="tmm-chart-legend"></div>
            <div class="download-bar">
              <span class="download-label">Export</span>
              <button id="tmm-dl-png" class="dl-btn" title="Download plot as PNG">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/><path d="m21 15-5-5L5 21"/></svg>
                PNG
              </button>
              <button id="tmm-dl-csv" class="dl-btn" title="Download this view's curves as CSV">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
                CSV
              </button>
              <button id="tmm-dl-share" class="dl-btn" title="Copy shareable link to clipboard">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg>
                Share
              </button>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="model-note card">
            <div class="model-note__header">
              <span>Notes</span>
              <span id="tmm-model-summary">Bragg mirror</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="tmm-note-list">
              <li id="tmm-note-text">
                Build a stack of homogeneous layers between a semi-infinite substrate
                (incidence side) and cladding (exit side). The spectrum shows reflectance
                and transmittance versus wavelength; the field view reconstructs the
                standing-wave amplitude through the structure at a single wavelength.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Editing layers.</strong> Set each layer's thickness,
                <em>n</em> and &kappa; in its box. The <strong>+</strong> button adds a
                copy directly below, the <strong>&uarr;/&darr;</strong> buttons reorder
                it, and <strong>&times;</strong> removes it.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Layer groups.</strong> Layers that share the same thickness,
                <em>n</em> and &kappa; form a <em>group</em> with the same colour. Click a
                layer's colour circle to <em>lock</em> the whole group &mdash; a black ring
                marks every member &mdash; so any edit to one entry applies to all of them
                at once. Click the same circle again to unlock, or click a different
                group's circle to switch the selection.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tmm-theory">
              <strong>Method.</strong> The transfer-matrix method propagates the
              tangential field through each homogeneous layer. The scalar field
              <em>F</em> is the in-plane field component that stays continuous across
              interfaces: <em>F</em> = E<sub>y</sub> for <strong>TE</strong> (s)
              polarization and <em>F</em> = H<sub>y</sub> for <strong>TM</strong> (p).
              Each layer uses &epsilon; = (n + i&kappa;)<sup>2</sup> and a normal
              wavevector k<sub>z</sub> = &radic;(k<sub>0</sub><sup>2</sup>&epsilon; &minus; k<sub>x</sub><sup>2</sup>),
              with k<sub>0</sub> = 2&pi;/&lambda; and the transverse wavevector
              k<sub>x</sub> = n<sub>s</sub> k<sub>0</sub> sin&theta; conserved across the stack.
              The angle of incidence &theta; is measured <em>inside</em> the incidence
              (substrate) medium n<sub>s</sub>.
              The 2&times;2 stack matrix M = m<sub>N</sub>&middot;&middot;&middot;m<sub>1</sub>
              yields the amplitude coefficients R, T and the powers
              &rho; = |R|<sup>2</sup> and &tau;. For a lossless stack &tau; + &rho; = 1.
            </p>
          </section>

